==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[Teutonick]]

===Etymology===
1580, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|Teutōnicus}}, from {{m|la|Teutōnes}}, {{term|Teutōnī|lang=la}} {{gloss|"the Teutons"; name of a Germanic tribe that inhabited coastal Germany and devastated Gaul between 113-101 B.C.}}. See {{term|Teuton|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˌtjuːˈtɒn.ɪk/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɒnɪk|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}
{{wikipedia}}

# Relating to the ancient [[Germanic]] people, the [[Teutons]].
# Having qualities that are regarded as typical of [[German]] people.
#: '''''Teutonic''' exactitude''
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} The [[Germanic]] branch of Indo-European family of languages

